  partName: Mounting Bolt (2)
  description: The Mounting Bolt (2) is a tiny, compact fastener positioned at the
    top-center-rear of the engine, constructed from Material.005, responsible for
    securing the engine to the vehicle's chassis, providing a stable and secure connection,
    and its compact shape enables efficient use of space. The Mounting Bolt (2) is
    designed to withstand significant stress and strain, ensuring the engine remains
    securely attached to the chassis. Notably, the Mounting Bolt (2) is designed
    to be easily removable and reusable, reducing maintenance time and costs.
